1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:52,020
Let's split up and replenish
our traveling supplies.

4
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,650
"Split up"? You've assigned me
most of the necessities.

5
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:58,900
Food, water, daily essentials.

6
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:02,280
What are you going to buy?

7
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,040
Herbs and stuff.

8
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:11,540
<i>That's the face she makes when
she's hiding something from me.</i>

9
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:14,880
<i>I've known Ms. Frieren for a long time.</i>

10
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:17,050
<i>Nothing good ever happens
when she makes that face.</i>

11
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,590
<i>She's definitely going to buy
something we don't need.</i>

12
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:23,470
I bought this.

13
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:25,060
What are you going to use that for?

14
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:28,060
This potion only dissolves clothing.

15
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,310
Go return it.

16
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:32,690
It's a book on magical history.
Classroom study is important, too.

17
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:39,360
<i>Well, I wouldn't call that one unnecessary.</i>

18
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,160
I'll meet you at the inn later.

19
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:55,960
<i>We can't afford to waste
our traveling funds.</i>

20
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:00,130
<i>I'd better keep a close eye on her.</i>

21
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:06,100
<i>An accessory shop?</i>

22
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:13,400
You went to sleep without
drying your hair again.

23
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:18,650
<i>So she's interested in fashion after all.</i>

24
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:25,740
<i>She seems really conflicted.</i>

25
00:03:27,450 --> 00:03:29,790
<i>What's with that face?</i>

26
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:34,580
<i>I've never seen Ms. Frieren
look so troubled before.</i>

27
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,860
<i>She spent a lot of time on that.</i>

28
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,030
<i>I suppose an accessory wouldn't hurt.</i>

29
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:07,740
<i>It's better than weird bones or medicines.</i>

30
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:14,540
<i>Maybe I'll resume my shopping soon.</i>

31
00:04:14,830 --> 00:04:18,040
Is there a shop around here
that sells good desserts?

32
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:21,170
<i>Now that's not fair.</i>

33
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:25,840
There's a tavern in the basement
of that building. Try asking there.

34
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:26,760
Thank you.

35
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:31,020
<i>I haven't eaten anything sweet in months!</i>

36
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:53,700
This must be it.

37
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:57,460
Is there a shop around here
that sells good desserts?

38
00:04:57,460 --> 00:05:01,250
<i>This clearly isn't the right
place to ask about desserts.</i>

39
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:05,550
A dessert joint? Who do you
think you're talking to?

40
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:09,050
<i>Gulp.</i>

41
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:13,720
You better believe this city's got
mountains of delicious desserts.

42
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:17,690
We can recommend you places all over.

43
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:20,560
<i>So they do know about desserts here.</i>

44
00:05:21,110 --> 00:05:23,780
For such rough-looking guys,
you know a lot about desserts.

45
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:27,700
A bit of sugar gives us the energy
we need to adventure.

46
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:34,830
Nothing beats rewarding yourself with
something sweet after a hard day's work.

47
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:32,870
<i>So they're adventurers. Though I'd say
even "rough" is an understatement.</i>

48
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:34,290
<i>They're terrifying.</i>

49
00:05:35,910 --> 00:05:37,250
See ya.

50
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:43,590
<i>Is she going to a dessert shop?</i>

51
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:51,510
<i>Huh? She's heading in
the direction of our inn.</i>

52
00:05:51,510 --> 00:05:53,100
<i>Is she going back?</i>

53
00:05:54,970 --> 00:05:57,180
<i>I'm not even close to finishing my shopping.</i>

54
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:01,980
You're late.

55
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:04,070
I'm sorry.

56
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:07,240
Well, no matter. Put your things down.

57
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:18,620
Shall we go get something sweet to eat?

58
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:37,640
What a nice view. No wonder
they recommended this place.

59
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:43,400
Ms. Frieren, I'm sorry for doubting you.

60
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:44,900
What are you talking about?

61
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,650
Nothing.

62
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,240
Choose whatever you'd like.

63
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,200
Can we afford it?

64
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:54,450
I've been saving up secretly.

65
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:57,490
<i>She's been keeping secret savings?</i>

66
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,790
Ms. Frieren, what will you have?

67
00:07:05,210 --> 00:07:08,300
Well, today I feel like...

68
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,180
Merkur pudding, right?

69
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:16,930
You feel like eating Merkur
pudding today, don't you?

70
00:07:17,390 --> 00:07:18,680
How did you know?

71
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:22,350
How many years do you think
we've traveled together?

72
00:07:22,350 --> 00:07:23,900
I can just tell.

73
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:32,070
I don't know anything about the rest of you.

74
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:35,950
Then maybe I'll try harder
to teach you about myself.

75
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:39,830
Incidentally, my favorite
food is Ruf-omelette.

76
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:42,830
Mine's grapes. The sourer, the better.

77
00:07:42,830 --> 00:07:44,040
Mine is—

78
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,790
Alcohol, right?

79
00:07:44,790 --> 00:07:47,380
I knew that already, you corrupt priest.

80
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,010
That's nothing to blush about.

81
00:07:50,010 --> 00:07:54,050
It's not a good sign that the one thing
she remembers is your drinking.

82
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,430
Fern, I'm sorry.

83
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:00,680
Why are you apologizing?

84
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:04,980
I don't know anything about you,

85
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:09,360
so I don't know what you like.

86
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:18,030
Come to think of it, it's my birthday today.

87
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,090
What a beautiful hair ornament.

88
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:34,630
Thank you. I'm delighted.

89
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:36,510
Really?

90
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:42,640
You seem to be hopelessly dense,
so let me be clear.

91
00:08:43,850 --> 00:08:48,900
I'm overjoyed that you
tried to get to know me.

92
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,400
Only because I tried?

93
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:59,780
You really don't understand
people's feelings, do you?

94
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,590
Shall we get going?

95
00:09:11,590 --> 00:09:12,170
Sure.

96
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:31,440
By the way, Ms. Frieren,
does this journey have a purpose?

97
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:36,190
Not particularly. I'm satisfying
my desire to collect spells.

98
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:40,620
But whenever possible,

99
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:44,160
I'd like to retrace the adventures
I had with Himmel and the others

100
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:47,080
before all sign of them fades away.

101
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:52,460
That's something important to you, right?

102
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:57,090
I don't know, so I'm trying
to figure that out.

103
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:06,140
You've finally grown taller than me.

104
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,980
I'm sixteen now. I could be your older sister.

105
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:11,980
My older sister?

106
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:16,570
Our diets are mostly the same,
so it can't be that.

107
00:10:17,190 --> 00:10:18,400
How strange.

108
00:10:50,350 --> 00:10:52,730
You've grown quite accustomed
to casting defensive spells.

109
00:10:55,270 --> 00:10:57,690
Let's put that into practice.

110
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,570
What?

111
00:11:08,450 --> 00:11:10,710
I aimed for the gaps in your defenses.

112
00:11:10,710 --> 00:11:13,040
If this had been a real battle, you'd be dead.

113
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:14,840
Now, then...

114
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,670
How will you handle this?

115
00:11:19,630 --> 00:11:20,670
Like this.

116
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:21,800
I see.

117
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,050
Can you withstand this?

118
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:35,310
That's enough for today.

119
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:48,200
Defensive magic is powerful,
but it rapidly depletes your mana.

120
00:11:48,990 --> 00:11:53,580
You'll exhaust your mana supply in seconds
if you try to maintain it over a large area.

121
00:11:55,250 --> 00:12:00,460
So the best option is to cast it in select
locations at the moment of impact.

122
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:01,550
Exactly.

123
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:07,930
Hup.

124
00:12:17,810 --> 00:12:20,690
We've been practicing nothing
but defensive magic.

125
00:12:20,690 --> 00:12:23,320
It directly improves your chances of survival.

126
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,450
You're right.

127
00:12:24,450 --> 00:12:28,410
A single defensive spell can defend
against most offensive spells.

128
00:12:28,910 --> 00:12:30,790
It's strange how powerful they are.

129
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:35,290
Fern, you haven't read the book on
magical history I gave you, have you?

130
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:39,500
Magic is about theory as much as practice.

131
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:45,590
I suppose I'll have to read
it to you at bedtime.

132
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:47,050
I'll read it myself.

133
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:49,300
I'm not a child, after all.

134
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:00,190
This village is where you wanted to go, right?

135
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:03,070
Are you here to collect odd spells again?

136
00:13:03,530 --> 00:13:06,070
No, not this time.

137
00:13:06,070 --> 00:13:08,370
Now it's up to the weather.

138
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:09,070
Yeah.

139
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:12,410
I have a question.

140
00:13:12,990 --> 00:13:14,000
It's an elf.

141
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:16,080
White hair...

142
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:20,340
Are you Ms. Frieren?

143
00:13:22,300 --> 00:13:23,800
How did you know?

144
00:13:26,170 --> 00:13:28,930
You're here to see the place where
Qual was sealed, aren't you?

145
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:31,760
I'll show you the way.

146
00:13:32,930 --> 00:13:34,020
Qual?

147
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,890
The Elder Sage of Corruption, Qual.

148
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:43,820
He's a demon who committed terrible
atrocities in this region eighty years ago,

149
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:48,860
before being sealed away
by Himmel the Hero and his party.

150
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:54,790
That seal will break soon,
so I'm here to defeat him,

151
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:56,870
but how did you know?

152
00:13:57,290 --> 00:13:59,540
I haven't told anyone about this.

153
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:06,800
Mr. Himmel visited this town every year
until about thirty years ago.

154
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:11,090
He was apparently checking
on the condition of the seal.

155
00:14:11,090 --> 00:14:13,050
He always was a softie.

156
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:16,930
He used to talk about you.

157
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:20,690
He called you heartless
for not checking on him.

158
00:14:21,190 --> 00:14:22,980
She's cold, isn't she?

159
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,690
Quite cold.

160
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:25,940
Sorry about that.

161
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:30,700
But she's not so heartless that
she'd leave the village to its fate.

162
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:34,830
She'll come when the seal is about to break.

163
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,460
That's what he said.

164
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:40,210
I see.

165
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:49,470
This is it?

166
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,820
It's become rather unstable.

167
00:15:06,690 --> 00:15:10,700
I'll dispel the seal tomorrow
and take care of Qual.

168
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:21,250
You're the one who sealed Qual, aren't you?

169
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:24,830
Is there a reason you did that?

170
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:28,840
He was simply too strong.

171
00:15:32,970 --> 00:15:34,510
I couldn't beat him.

172
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:39,560
Even among the Demon King's forces,
Qual was an exceptional mage.

173
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:45,730
He developed the first piercing spell
in history, which he called Zoltraak.

174
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:51,900
It pierced not only defensive spells but
the magic resistance of armor as well.

175
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:54,610
It directly targeted and destroyed the body.

176
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:58,790
It's said that in this region,

177
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:04,250
40% of adventurers and 70% of mages
were killed by Zoltraak.

178
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:09,880
That's too powerful.

179
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:14,510
Yes, it was. Much too powerful.

180
00:16:15,390 --> 00:16:18,760
And that's why it backfired on him.

181
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:21,180
What do you mean?

182
00:16:25,730 --> 00:16:28,270
You really haven't read that
history tome, have you?

183
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:31,150
Are you sure I shouldn't read it to you?

184
00:16:31,150 --> 00:16:32,740
I'll start reading it right now.

185
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:34,990
No, it's fine.

186
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:38,280
It's more important that
you get a good night's sleep.

187
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:41,080
You'll see tomorrow, anyway.

188
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:48,670
I'm dispelling the seal.

189
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,420
Don't let your guard down.

190
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:23,750
It's been a while, Frieren.

191
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,580
How many years has it been?

192
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,330
Eighty.

193
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:32,090
A mere eighty years, huh?

194
00:17:32,090 --> 00:17:34,010
For us, anyway.

195
00:17:35,590 --> 00:17:37,680
And the Demon King?

196
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,890
We killed him.

197
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:40,800
I see.

198
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:46,270
Then I shall avenge him.

199
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:48,770
Fern, cast a defensive spell in front of us.

200
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:51,820
Zoltraak!

201
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:02,780
I'm surprised.

202
00:18:03,330 --> 00:18:05,790
You blocked Zoltraak.

203
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:11,170
That defensive spell of yours
must be powerful indeed.

204
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:16,010
Ms. Frieren, what's going on?

205
00:18:17,090 --> 00:18:19,680
That was ordinary offensive magic.

206
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,180
That's Zoltraak.

207
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:27,810
The killing magic he developed.

208
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:35,820
Qual, your magic was simply too powerful.

209
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:45,200
After you were sealed away, mages across
the land studied and analyzed Zoltraak.

210
00:18:46,290 --> 00:18:51,670
In just a few years, Zoltraak was
incorporated into humankind's magic system,

211
00:18:51,670 --> 00:18:56,880
and powerful new defensive spells
were developed.

212
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:02,590
The magic resistance offered by equipment
has improved significantly as well,

213
00:19:03,010 --> 00:19:06,470
making Zoltraak no longer killing magic.

214
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:11,060
Now it's just "ordinary offensive magic."

215
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:18,440
Eighty years is quite a long time for humans.

216
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:22,950
Qual, if you don't resist,
I'll make your death painless.

217
00:19:23,950 --> 00:19:25,330
I see.

218
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,200
I see, I see.

219
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:34,460
It attunes itself to the offensive
magic and disperses its power.

220
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,750
A complex spell indeed.

221
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:42,130
It must consume a great deal of mana.

222
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:45,090
He figured out the weakness
of defensive magic.

223
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:47,930
Fern, you know what to do, right?

224
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:51,850
Yes. I saw it in our practices.

225
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:55,100
Then protect me as well.

226
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:24,630
So you can fly? Interesting.

227
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:26,550
Zoltraak.

228
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:43,650
Frieren... My spell...

229
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:03,340
Now we can live in peace.

230
00:21:04,130 --> 00:21:06,430
That hat...

231
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,300
This thing?

232
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:13,930
Around here, the sun's rays are strong
even at this time of year,

233
00:21:13,930 --> 00:21:16,020
so all farmers wear them.

234
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:19,270
I've seen this hat before.

235
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:29,740
You're the brat who flipped my skirt up.

236
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:31,780
Take that!

237
00:21:33,790 --> 00:21:36,960
What do you think you're doing, brat?

238
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:40,080
I'll kill you! You saw what I've
been wanting to see all this time!

239
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:41,670
You'd better not kill him.

240
00:21:41,670 --> 00:21:44,130
I'll show you mine.

241
00:21:44,130 --> 00:21:45,130
Yikes.

242
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:51,050
You're still alive.

243
00:21:51,850 --> 00:21:54,810
Thanks to you,
I'll be able to live even longer.

244
00:21:55,640 --> 00:22:00,060
I'm glad I trusted Himmel's words and waited.

245
00:22:10,110 --> 00:22:13,450
Ms. Frieren, they thanked you.

246
00:22:13,950 --> 00:22:15,950
They didn't thank me.

247
00:22:17,330 --> 00:22:21,080
The people of this village
believed in Himmel.

248
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:29,470
I don't understand, exactly,
but I think Mr. Himmel believed in you.

249
00:22:34,310 --> 00:22:35,810
What is it?

250
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:37,310
Nothing.

251
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:22,740
Because I felt sorry for you.

252
00:24:20,820 --> 00:24:23,740
Because it's more convenient that way.

253
00:24:21,530 --> 00:24:24,870
She was an irresponsible person.

254
00:24:23,990 --> 00:24:25,740
That's enough depressing talk.

255
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:26,410
Are you sure you haven't been
around since prehistoric times?

256
00:24:24,870 --> 00:24:27,080
You're more conscientious than you look.

257
00:24:25,740 --> 00:24:27,080
It was a long time ago.

258
00:24:26,410 --> 00:24:30,160
Aureole, the land where souls rest.
